[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77543"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${A}^{′}$, the image of $A(-1,1)$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $A$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $A:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${A}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${A}^{′}(2,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-275707/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "948a5b29-8e1a-50af-a988-46d5e041bafd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275707/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "93aa8ab5-5591-5f08-b447-a0aef4fe6aef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275707/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-275707/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275707/field-2/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "6002c463-4ff4-5d69-acba-d6222dabf0b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275707/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8fba06d-6cd2-5644-bbad-00c49cefb939" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275707/field-2/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer-field/choices ["q-275707/field-2/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275707" :question/id #uuid "06ad069c-d38e-5402-9689-521e2de3e981" :question/math-academy-id "q-275707" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${C}^{′}$, the image of $C(0,3)$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${C}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $C$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $C:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${C}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${C}^{′}(0,-12).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-275707/field-1" "q-275707/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275707"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281092/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "8c893013-185f-54bd-b66c-4675a362b271" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281092/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "168b0936-3a1f-55f4-a451-0872dda0b26c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281092/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b1712d5-29ee-514d-98f7-f5657aaedf01" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281092/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-281092/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-281092/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281092/field-2/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "d05342c9-2d35-5f2c-92b5-e68831deef8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281092/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5400f69-bbed-5e2f-bc84-609736a8b886" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281092/field-2/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-281092/field-2/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281092" :question/id #uuid "9977333f-4553-552c-b0da-170e12a20347" :question/math-academy-id "q-281092" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${Y}^{′}$, the image of $Y(-2,-3)$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${Y}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $Y$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $Y:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${Y}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${Y}^{′}(-2,11).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281092/field-1" "q-281092/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281092"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281085/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "befd7c5b-0baf-531e-8321-c183994f4b1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281085/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a22b5dec-c7e3-5f42-83e0-c25d7f942881" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281085/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-281085/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281085/field-2/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "01aad24e-492d-5b78-9d51-c044bf180822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281085/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f6e0366-e26e-5225-9ac3-f3990a2cb148" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281085/field-2/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer-field/choices ["q-281085/field-2/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281085" :question/id #uuid "de6b08c0-664a-50ea-b427-adc41330b5b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281085" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S(2,-1)$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${S}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $S:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${S}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${S}^{′}(14,-7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-281085/field-1" "q-281085/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281085"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77722/selection/4ec4dbda2081a25eb39e5c54be41fffc44e2d0516a4b93b95619181850a8f9ad" :answer/id #uuid "14e08eb5-6564-5320-ba3e-800ac3c4ee02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77722/selection/144b9b27e5407875a6110661fb7cd60e576017bb9ef58d532f3de14f6cf246b2" :answer/id #uuid "95de2d9a-d163-5770-a741-02b6d9cd9188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77722/selection/75f4af1a631ad1eb2c776bcfc360da05b1f0db1e66e0cdeeac4b794c54d527b2" :answer/id #uuid "e2404d92-199e-5d01-ae9c-ab5eaa74aeb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(6,-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77722/selection/3b2c46ffb542d8d861157b97b82d5b575d7d496d3d5fb4b6a50ad59648a23aa5" :answer/id #uuid "111a8184-54d9-5473-aef8-a922b4e99a4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "