-fields ["q-77722/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281130/field-1/5f36dcd7ab24104a67ea76a46c1471bc3af678b5baff92d77f8309d4a858136d" :answer/id #uuid "ab2cc4f3-7790-5ea8-84ac-826e6fcb166e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7x+10y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281130/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d280eba-bd43-5257-80cf-1cea230f9f70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281130/field-1/5f36dcd7ab24104a67ea76a46c1471bc3af678b5baff92d77f8309d4a858136d" :answer-field/choices ["q-281130/field-1/5f36dcd7ab24104a67ea76a46c1471bc3af678b5baff92d77f8309d4a858136d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281130" :question/id #uuid "8680e675-b4fd-563b-ae15-e54ded036ebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-281130" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-81.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-3$ passes through the points $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-5)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-3,-6)$ and ${B}^{′}(7,-13).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{-13+6}{7-(-3)}(x+3) \\\\ y+6 & =-\\frac{7}{10}(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10y+60 & =-7x-21 \\\\ 7x+10y & =-81\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281130/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281241/field-1/e60d21c1edc1a1b0e54e4a576b7a72542c73c6f5897df42d39415a69184dc369" :answer/id #uuid "1c386580-ca9b-5585-927b-9e48bb3efc39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281241/field-1/7f61fb36a9b984a34a71f7d90dcab60bd27ee29007c3cbb4a799aad4a2560802" :answer/id #uuid "b9e5ef69-3db1-5b33-b94a-01a970e22ab3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281241/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7fade406-2413-58fb-9633-e853709b7243" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281241/field-1/e60d21c1edc1a1b0e54e4a576b7a72542c73c6f5897df42d39415a69184dc369" :answer-field/choices ["q-281241/field-1/e60d21c1edc1a1b0e54e4a576b7a72542c73c6f5897df42d39415a69184dc369" "q-281241/field-1/7f61fb36a9b984a34a71f7d90dcab60bd27ee29007c3cbb4a799aad4a2560802"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281241" :question/id #uuid "dc073c03-011e-5148-854c-72e20d7fe7f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-281241" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=2x+1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=2x+1$ passes through the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-1,1)$ and ${B}^{′}(0,5).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{5-1}{0+1}(x+1) \\\\ y-1 & =4(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-1 & =4x+4 \\\\ 4x-y & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281241/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281241"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77781/selection/276e873d7c1aaf5a28294e37349ce8c53ab8ac04d6a2725ea4a1dc2109371ac2" :answer/id #uuid "dd71dbb6-3925-5ba6-a29f-e54e70b26c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-3y+15=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77781/selection/d7ea4e5df564e1e6dc177eb6ad1d28574386524a075f66e7a83bff23fb509a2a" :answer/id #uuid "06ba1015-6c65-526a-af09-2d93a24c4a