hrough the points $C(0,3)$ and $L(1,4)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $C$ and $L$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${C}^{′}(-3,3)$ and ${L}^{′}(0,5).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${C}^{′}$ and ${L}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{5-3}{0-(-3)}(x-(-3)) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{2}{3}(x+3) \\\\ 3y-9 & =2x+6 \\\\ 2x-3y+15 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77781/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77781"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770/selection/2ce5ac1290e4a62c374eb90a6896623b949d49db661ff1359c9dcfae2be12216" :answer/id #uuid "9d2a45a7-1d56-5972-a3ae-b229bdf91a0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13x+2y+30=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770/selection/9751b3ce175bd47cef7b570f63b83f7f03de2f8cda91a564d574d9ab9f363f59" :answer/id #uuid "4c42e312-9022-5fae-9d2e-b674d6c5f486" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12x+y+5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770/selection/603729029ccc8453a41d72a740427fa59ea6e62a89397211946e7902e73dc084" :answer/id #uuid "62b3b6f8-608f-553a-ab97-245f48224806" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y+5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770/selection/db2188cfa04596ab59ba567cb070a4bba09adcdc32eacf32b46566cb28916464" :answer/id #uuid "c95046fc-1f7f-5094-b76e-4eac15a2afa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770/selection/6ff99df435abb397c47c2758f38e7d96424102aa09372ac420540c8269e5efc4" :answer/id #uuid "dd292873-51a7-5190-8a5f-25935b5b587f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x+y-15=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4cb4c72-f05b-580e-95f4-b36b7f2b6671" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77770/selection/2ce5ac1290e4a62c374eb90a6896623b949d49db661ff1359c9dcfae2be12216" :answer-field/choices ["q-77770/selection/2ce5ac1290e4a62c374eb90a6896623b949d49db661ff1359c9dcfae2be12216" "q-77770/selection/9751b3ce175bd47cef7b570f63b83f7f03de2f8cda91a564d574d9ab9f363f59" "q-77770/selection/603729029ccc8453a41d72a740427fa59ea6e62a89397211946e7902e73dc084" "q-77770/selection/db2188cfa04596ab59ba567cb070a4bba09adcdc32eacf32b46566cb28916464" "q-77770/selection/6ff99df435abb397c47c2758f38e7d96424102aa09372ac420540c8269e5efc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77770" :question/id #uuid "4afad73e-00dd-5eda-b478-328fd2031846" :question/math-academy-id "q-77770" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=4x+5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=4x+5$ passes through the points $G(0,5)$ and $H(1,9)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $G$ and $H$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -15 & -28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${G}^{′}(0,-15)$ and ${H}^{′}(2,-28).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${G}^{′}$ and ${H}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-15) & =\\frac{-28-(-15)}{2-0}(x-0) \\\\ y+15 & =-\\frac{13}{2}x \\\\ 2y+30 & =-13x \\\\ 13x+2y+30 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77770/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779/selection/fc9a682a582113a09b43a23bdd15c5365715e3960173ff481b647468e75ae87f" :answer/id #uuid "b1dcd5a0-96e6-545c-98e6-81fa6a9fa489" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y-8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779/selection/0578043400931253eb7e3c82fb0c5b37d82f7f2397572841cbe45ae11e2db0b0" :answer/id #uuid "dc0b484c-2cfd-5a55-ac48-2f380cf6db30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y-24=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779/selection/f20ce6aaca009a5ef12ef10c8ae390d3e13a56c87612e704931b71db1f80cc4d" :answer/id #uuid "961c3500-d27e-5d7e-8f61-763a2f32afa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-y+24=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779/selection/daf23da22c52907c58714ee1f0f94bf2088ef7c1bb4417cd7ac1d80cc1a28cd3" :answer/id #uuid "69bf48e6-a1ee-55fa-95a1-6c28604cf206" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+y+24=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779/selection/460008188c257d1f5af65dc95ee41f5993eacd11d3db32bbcc83b9605a0c288c" :answer/id #uuid "bb13ebfe-dea1-5938-91f8-531d04e871bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-y+8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "628a0264-aaab-5f5b-8bdb-30974343600d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77779/selection/0578043400931253eb7e3c82fb0c5b37d82f7f2397572841cbe45ae11e2db0b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-77779/selection/fc9a682a582113a09b43a23bdd15c5365715e3960173ff481b647468e75ae87f" "q-77779/selection/0578043400931253eb7e3c82fb0c5b37d82f7f2397572841cbe45ae11e2db0b0" "q-77779/selection/f20ce6aaca009a5ef12ef10c8ae390d3e13a56c87612e704931b71db1f80cc4d" "q-77779/selection/daf23da22c52907c58714ee1f0f94bf2088ef7c1bb4417cd7ac1d80cc1a28cd3" "q-77779/selection/460008188c257d1f5af65dc95ee41f5993eacd11d3db32bbcc83b9605a0c288c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77779" :question/id #uuid "2e1d4b30-c2f9-5d8e-ac8c-cb94e781f714" :question/math-academy-id "q-77779" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=-x-4$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=-x-4$ passes through the points $W(0,-4)$ and $Z(1,-5)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $W$ and $Z$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${W}^{′}(8,0)$ and ${Z}^{′}(9,-3).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${W}^{′}$ and ${Z}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{-3-0}{9-8}(x-8) \\\\ y & =-3(x-8) \\\\ y & =-3x+24 \\\\ 3x+y-24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275719/field-1/b4685d1d65d082290443f13eed9bb91fd9464095408520ab924ab2f3f4b105c7" :answer/id #uuid "6a4390ea-6347-5152-885b-ce7f60e0b73c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-17y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275719/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b9634137-e64d-5b61-a9e1-5d0760d323e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275719/field-1/b4685d1d65d082290443f13eed9bb91fd9464095408520ab924ab2f3f4b105c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-275719/field-1/b4685d1d65d082290443f13eed9bb91fd9464095408520ab924ab2f3f4b105c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275719" :question/id #uuid "809b9f25-344f-56b6-953a-27ba29139b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275719" :question/problem "Consider the line $4x-y-3=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=27.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $4x-y-3=0$ passes through the points $U(0,-3)$ and $V(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $U$ and $V$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${U}^{′}(-12,-3)$ and ${V}^{′}(5,-1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =\\frac{-1-(-3)}{5-(-12)}(x-(-12)) \\\\ y+3 & =\\frac{2}{17}(x+12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+3 & =\\frac{2}{17}(x+12) \\\\ 17y+51 & =2x+24 \\\\ 51-24 & =2x-17y \\\\ 2x-17y & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-275719/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275719"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77653"] :question/problem "Consider the line $2x+y-3=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $2x+y-3=0$ passes through the points $A(0,3)$ and $B(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(0,6)$ and ${B}^{′}(-2,3).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-6 & =\\frac{3-6}{-2-0}(x-0) \\\\ y-6 & =\\frac{3}{2}x \\\\ 2y-12 & =3x \\\\ 3x-2y+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-275715/field-1/f02822b53b5f80541b098aee7a5b3cb801293e8687385a424b287ada50425dba" :answer/id #uuid "68799dea-8b4b-5baa-82ed-44d2e3534b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275715/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b401204d-43a4-5fb8-b29c-dac1df78bf81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275715/field-1/f02822b53b5f80541b098aee7a5b3cb801293e8687385a424b287ada50425dba" :answer-field/choices ["q-275715/field-1/f02822b53b5f80541b098aee7a5b3cb801293e8687385a424b287ada50425dba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275715" :question/id #uuid "e1cb83ff-f76b-5d38-a9f8-094d98adaff6" :question/math-academy-id "q-275715" :question/problem "Consider the line $x=-2$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=14.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $x=-2$ passes through the points $G(-2,0)$ and $H(-2,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $G$ and $H$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${G}^{′}(2,-6)$ and ${H}^{′}(6,-4).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-6) & =\\frac{-4-(-6)}{6-2}(x-2) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-2) \\\\ 2y+12 & =x-2 \\\\ 12+2 & =x-2y \\\\ x-2y & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275715/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275715"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281586/field-1/f3ad00044c999f0b8eeb36ef9c36ab03fb9693cb7a3bf5d291ce4315687949f4" :answer/id #uuid "730fcfe2-2009-559c-bcd5-59d421a033b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x-7y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281586/field-1/811caf99b7dbb34c072520f73d468461c1d5252213d62e32595e2f79324b4972" :answer/id #uuid "c3f57e7e-1a4e-506c-8c8f-f93617e872c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+7y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281586/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "48df28e7-8f48-5d7a-9e4d-34bfe8c30265" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281586/field-1/f3ad00044c999f0b8eeb36ef9c36ab03fb9693cb7a3bf5d291ce4315687949f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-281586/field-1/f3ad00044c999f0b8eeb36ef9c36ab03fb9693cb7a3bf5d291ce4315687949f4" "q-281586/field-1/811caf99b7dbb34c072520f73d468461c1d5252213d62e32595e2f79324b4972"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281586" :question/id #uuid "534b0fc4-23b0-567d-ab9e-8474a8eb5bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281586" :question/problem "Consider the line $-4x+y+1=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $-4x+y+1=0$ passes through the points $P(0,-1)$ and $Q(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(-1,-2)$ and ${Q}^{′}(6,6).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+2 & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{6-(-1)}(x+1) \\\\ y+2 & =\\frac{8}{7}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y+14 & =8x+8 \\\\ 8x-7y & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n8x-7y=6\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-281586/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281583/field-1/05467d187805c5f88fdfdbcae5fa8dce85917ccb22929b62a18de77bce0705c0" :answer/id #uuid "9c6784ba-0bcf-5132-b031-9ca99c91e25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+5y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdbd96d5-67fa-52eb-9b72-b1a6da45dacd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281583/field-1/05467d187805c5f88fdfdbcae5fa8dce85917ccb22929b62a18de77bce0705c0" :answer-field/choices ["q-281583/field-1/05467d187805c5f88fdfdbcae5fa8dce85917ccb22929b62a18de77bce0705c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281583" :question/id #uuid "91f5a824-ec1d-58a0-a686-86bca0afba26" :question/math-academy-id "q-281583" :question/problem "Consider the line $3x+2y-6=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=42.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $3x+2y-6=0$ passes through the points $P(0,3)$ and $Q(2,0)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(9,-6)$ and ${Q}^{′}(4,2).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-6) & =\\frac{2-(-6)}{4-9}(x-9) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{8}{-5}(x-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =-\\frac{8}{5}(x-9) \\\\ 5y+30 & =-8x+72 \\\\ 8x+5y & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n8x+5y=42\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-281583/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6704"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $B',$ the image of $B(2,-3)$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $B$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a column vector $\\mathbf{x}$ containing the coordinates of $B{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $T\\mathbf{x}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $T \\mathbf{x},$ contains the coordinates of $B'.$ Therefore, $B'(3,-5).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6713"] :question/problem "Consider the line $y=3x-2$ and linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find two points on the given line. Substituting $x=0$ and $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0\\, & \\to \\,y=3(0)-2=-2, \\\\ x=1\\, & \\to \\,y=3(1)-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two points on the line, $P(0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1).$\n\nTo find the images of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$ in its columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are $P'(0,-2)$ and $Q'(-1,4).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through $P'$ and $Q'\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{4-(-2)}{-1-0}(x-0) \\\\ y+2 & =-6x \\\\ 6x+y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6705"] :question/problem "Consider the line $5x-y-3=0$ and linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find two points on the given line. Solving for $y,$ we get $y=5x-3,$ and substituting $x=0$ and $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0\\, & \\to \\,y=5(0)-3=-3, \\\\ x=1\\, & \\to \\,y=5(1)-3=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two points on the line, $P(0,-3)$ and $Q(1,2).$\n\nTo find the images of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$ in its columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are $P'(-3,-6)$ and $Q'(-1,3).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through $P'$ and $Q'\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-6) & =\\frac{3-(-6)}{-1-(-3)}(x-(-3)) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{9}{2}(x+3) \\\\ 2y+12 & =9x+27 \\\\ 9x-2y+15 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
